All compensation networks~\cite{gautam2026fastforward} were trained for 1000 steps (lr=$10^{-4}$, batch size 4, seq length 2048). Training loss plateaus by step 700 across all valid runs: 30\% s42 (final loss 0.70), 30\% s456 (0.68), 50\% s42 (1.07), with fluctuations remaining within 0.08 loss units for the final 300 steps. The compensation network converges but provides no quality improvement over the KL predictor alone, confirming that the redundancy result reflects predictor self-sufficiency rather than insufficient compensation training. % exp_id: kl_comp_30_s42, kl_comp_30_s456, kl_comp_50_s42


\section{Qwen-2.5-14B Detailed Results}
\label{app:14b}

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Qwen-2.5-14B at 30\% nominal sparsity. Actual sparsity differs: KL 29.6\% (3-seed), TEAL 29.3\% (target 30\%). \textbf{Bold}: best sparse per column per group. BCE collapses to 6.4\% native sparsity (\S\ref{sec:method:gradient}), so forced global top-$k$ is used.}
\label{tab:14b}
\small
\resizebox{\columnwidth}{!}{
\begin{tabular}{lcccccccc}
\toprule
Method & PPL$\downarrow$ & ARC-c & WG & MMLU & GSM8K & HS & PIQA \\
\midrule
Dense & 5.19 & 67.58 & 81.06 & 79.77 & 87.57 & 84.20 & 81.94 \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{8}{l}{\emph{Global top-$k$ allocation}} \\
KL (Ours) & \textbf{7.62} & 57.17 & 72.06 & 63.72 & 48.82 & \textbf{75.01} & \textbf{77.37} \\ % exp_id: qwen14b_kl30_s42
TEAL & 8.73 & 56.83 & \textbf{72.69} & \textbf{71.83} & 49.51 & 70.51 & 74.70 \\ % exp_id: qwen14b_teal30_eval
BCE & 8.76 & \textbf{57.59} & 72.61 & 71.67 & \textbf{53.07} & 53.43 & 68.28 \\ % exp_id: qwen14b_bce30_s42_eval
\midrule
\multicolumn{8}{l}{\emph{Uniform allocation}} \\
KL (Ours) & \textbf{7.90} & 53.50 & \textbf{72.82} & 63.55 & 32.1$\pm$5.2 & \textbf{71.67$\pm$1.0} & \textbf{75.06$\pm$0.2} \\ % exp_id: qwen14b_kl30_uniform (v3/v5 3-seed)
TEAL & 8.01 & \textbf{55.29} & 69.85 & \textbf{66.34} & \textbf{52.1} & 67.72 & 74.70 \\ % exp_id: qwen14b_teal30_uniform
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}}
\end{table}

Under global allocation, BCE's HellaSwag drops to 53.43\% ($-$17pp vs.\ TEAL), indicating that the magnitude-based predictor's mask quality degrades severely when combined with non-uniform budget distribution at 14B scale. % exp_id: qwen14b_bce30_s42_eval, qwen14b_teal30_eval

